Problem: Longest Valid Parentheses (LC 32)

Pattern:
Stack + Index Tracking

Approach:

1. Create a stack to store indices of brackets.
2. Push -1 initially as a base index before the string starts.
3. Traverse the string from left to right.
4. If the current character is an opening bracket, push its index into the stack.
5. If the current character is a closing bracket, pop the top index.
6. If the stack becomes empty after popping, push the current index as the new boundary.
7. Otherwise, calculate the current valid length using current index minus the index at the top of the stack.
8. Keep updating the maximum length found.
9. Return the maximum length after processing the complete string.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(n)
